[h1]v0.1.20 - Bushes no longer stop strong cars[/h1]

[h2]What you need to do[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]ZombieBuddy users:[/b] nothing, Steam updates the mod and the fix comes with it.
[*][b]Manual install:[/b] copy the zombie folder from B42.21_Manual_Install over your old one again (one class changed).
[*][b]Dedicated servers:[/b] nothing, servers still need no Java install.
[/list]

[h2]Changes[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Driving into a bush no longer stops a strong car.[/b] The base game takes a share of your speed away for as long as you touch a bush, and it does not care how strong the engine is, so even a very powerful car ended up crawling in a hedge. The Foliage shove option now starts from a much lower base: a weak engine is still slowed by bushes, a strong one drives straight through. Raise the option if you want the base game's behaviour back, set it to 0 for no effect. Zombies are not affected by this.
[/list]

This came from a report of a heavy car stopping dead in a bush. If your car still crawls on plain dirt or gravel, tell me which car it is and what the mechanics window says for its engine power and weight.
